		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">0</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Suppose we have to rotate array only 1 time, what will happen to last element of array?
Option 1: It will be removed from array, since there is no place in right to shift it.
Option 2: It will be shifted to index 0, since first element is moved to index 1, so there is empty space at index 0.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">1244.1867063492064</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">310.989710620874</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">206.81735838214126</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">138.41669313352313</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Suppose we have to rotate array only 1 time, what will happen to last element of array?
Option 1: It will be removed from array, since there is no place in right to shift it.
Option 2: It will be shifted to index 0, since first element is moved to index 1, so there is empty space at index 0.</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
