		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">40</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As I process 1000 values, it will be difficult for me to remember all the numbers, so I will write down all the numbers in a paper.
2. Then I will take remainder after dividing m from length of array, lets say it n.
3. Then I will see what was the index of the element previously which is now at the first index, then I will start writing all the element starting from that element to the end of the array.
4. Still I don't have those elements which are before that element which is now at index 0. So, now I wrote all elements starting from the element which is at index 0 previously upto the element which is now at index 0.
5. Here I have observed that when length of array is 1000 and m%(length of array) === 200 then the index 0 position element is at index 200 after final rotation. Similary when m%(length of array) ===3 then final index position of first element is 3.
6. Also the element which is at index 800 previously, is at starting position now, i.e 1000-800 (or length of array - m%(length of array)). Similary for all previous test cases.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">83.23868211388123</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">3183.526270761844</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">594.6604286268145</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">254.482998015921</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As I process 1000 values, it will be difficult for me to remember all the numbers, so I will write down all the numbers in a paper.
2. Then I will take remainder after dividing m from length of array, lets say it n.
3. Then I will see what was the index of the element previously which is now at the first index, then I will start writing all the element starting from that element to the end of the array.
4. Still I don't have those elements which are before that element which is now at index 0. So, now I wrote all elements starting from the element which is at index 0 previously upto the element which is now at index 0.
5. Here I have observed that when length of array is 1000 and m%(length of array) === 200 then the index 0 position element is at index 200 after final rotation. Similary when m%(length of array) ===3 then final index position of first element is 3.
6. Also the element which is at index 800 previously, is at starting position now, i.e 1000-800 (or length of array - m%(length of array)). Similary for all previous test cases.</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
