		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">41</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I came up with.

1. Read the array.
2. Read the value m.
3. Create a variable called len for storing the length of array
4. Calculate remainder after dividing m from len. (why not m minus len)
5. Create a variable called rotations and store the value m%len in it.
6. Create a variable called startIndex to store the position of the index which is at index 0 now. Used startIndex = len - rotation.
7. Now display the number which is at index startIndex,then move to next index.
8. Repeat step 7 till we reach end of the array.
9. Now display element which is at index 0, and move to next index.
10. Repeat line 9 till we reach the index startIndex.</attribute>
